# Capacitor shell — derived and local-only artifacts (L1-P1).
#
# native/android/ IS committed: it carries the application id, the backup
# hardening that holds half of LSC-P1-INV-002, and the Gradle pins. None of
# that survives regeneration, so it is source, not output. Its own generated
# .gitignore (native/android/.gitignore) already excludes the build outputs and
# the copies `cap sync` writes into it.
#
# www/ is NOT committed: it is a byte-identical copy of files that already live
# in app/, assembled by tools/stage-webdir.js. Committing it would duplicate
# every shipped byte and create a second place for them to drift. `cap sync`
# must therefore be preceded by a stage run — `npm run sync` does both.

node_modules/
www/

# Gradle / APK output that native/android/.gitignore does not already cover
# from this level.
*.apk
*.aab

# Signing material. Nothing in this packet produces a release key (debug
# signing only), and nothing ever commits one.
*.jks
*.keystore
